.TH SAMPLE 1
.SH NAME
sample, example \- a page to try the macros of man(6) on
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sample
[
.B -cds
] [
.B -o
.I file
] [
.I name ...
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Sample
does nothing: it is a page written to be typeset.
Its first paragraph is long enough to be put on several lines, so that one sees where a line is ended when the next word does not fit.
A sentence ends here.
Not after e.g.\&
this one, nor after
.B a.out
in the font of what is typed; it does after
.BR one .
A word with a hyphen may be cut after it, as in a twenty-seven-letter
right-to-left never-ending word; not an option's, as
.BR -long-option-name-that-is-not-to-be-cut-anywhere-in-its-letters ,
and not a minus:
.BR \-5 .
.PP
The options are:
.TP
.B -c
Complement the set.
A tag shorter than its width has its text on its line.
.TP
.B -d
Delete.
.TP
.BI -o " file"
The tag is wider than five letters: its text starts below.
.TP 12
.B -s
Squeeze, with a width said.
.TP
.B -t
The width stays.
.PD 0
.TP
.B -u
.TP
.B -v
Two tags, one text, closed up.
.PD
.PP
A paragraph, then one further right:
.IP
Indented, with no tag.
.IP \(bu 3
With a bullet.
.RS
.PP
Inside a relative indent,
.L quoted
and
.LR typed ,
the fonts in turn:
.IR troff (1),
.RB [ -x ]
and
.SM SMALL .
.RE
.PP
Back at the margin.
.SS A subsection
.HP
A hanging paragraph has its first line at the margin and the others to its right, which shows only when it is long enough to have others.
.PP
Lines that are not filled:
.IP
.EX
int	n;	/* a tab, then another */
char	*name;
	for(i = 0; i < n; i++)
		print("%d\en", i);
.EE
.PP
With stops of its own
.RI ( .ta ):
.nf
.ta 10n +6n
name	size	what
tr	12	translate
.fi
.DT
.PP
A line moved by hand,
.br
a break,
.sp 2
and two lines' space.
.ti +4
One line further right, and the rest of this paragraph back where it was, as long as it takes to see it.
.in +3
The margin moved,
.in
and back.
.ce
centered
.SH EXAMPLES
A character by its name: \(em, \(bu, \(->, 2\(mu3; a backslash: \e;
\fIitalic\fP, \fLtyped\fR and \s-2smaller\s0.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR troff (1),
.IR man (6)
